<section class="drawing-workspace" aria-labelledby="drawing-heading" id="tm-drawings">
 <p class="eyebrow">DRAWINGS &amp; LAYOUTS</p><h2 id="drawing-heading">Choose how to add your drawing</h2>
 <div class="choices"><a href="#tm-create"><strong>1. Create a drawing</strong><span>Generate a starting layout automatically, then edit it manually. Export DXF or PDF.</span></a><a href="#tm-upload"><strong>2. Upload an existing drawing</strong><span>Choose DXF, DWG, PDF or an image. Preview supported files and download the unchanged original.</span></a></div>
 <p class="draft"><strong>Draft layouts only.</strong> Generated layouts are schematic and not to scale. A competent traffic-management designer must review them against the actual site and applicable standards before use. Symbols are illustrative; calculated distances apply only to the supported rule profile and still need site verification. Signal timings and design approval are not calculated.</p>
 <section id="tm-create" aria-labelledby="create-heading"><h3 id="create-heading">Create a drawing</h3>
 <p>Your layout autosaves in <strong>this browser on this device</strong>, where browser storage is available. It is not saved to your account, sent to our server or attached to a paid work pack. Clearing browser data can erase it. Export DXF or PDF to keep a file; save a project to reopen and edit it later.</p>
 <form data-generator class="generator">
 <h4>Calculate a draft → edit it manually</h4><p>Calculate a core layout for two-way portable signals on a two-lane single carriageway, or one-lane static closures on a 2–4 lane dual carriageway/motorway. Enter surveyed dimensions and the <strong>permanent</strong> speed limit. This is design assistance, not authority approval.</p>
 <div class="generator-fields">
 <label>Road name<input name="roadName" maxlength="80" placeholder="London Road"></label>
 <label>Road / layout<select name="roadType"><option value="single">Single carriageway — two-way signals</option><option value="dual">Dual carriageway — one-lane closure</option><option value="motorway">Motorway — one-lane closure</option></select></label>
 <label>Permanent speed limit (mph)<select name="speed"><option value="20">20</option><option value="30" selected>30</option><option value="40">40</option><option value="50">50</option><option value="60">60</option><option value="70">70</option></select></label>
 <label>Lanes on the modelled carriageway<select name="laneCount"><option value="2">2</option><option value="3">3</option><option value="4">4</option></select></label>
 <label>Closed side in increasing-chainage direction<select name="worksSide"><option value="near">Nearside / left</option><option value="off">Offside / right</option></select></label>
 <label>Width of modelled carriageway (m)<input name="roadWidth" type="number" min="3" max="25" step="any" required placeholder="Both lanes for signals; one direction for dual"></label>
 <label>Working-space width, excluding safety clearance (m)<input name="workWidth" type="number" min="0.5" max="10" step="any" required placeholder="Includes plant and material working space"></label>
 <label>Working-space length (m)<input name="worksLength" type="number" min="1" max="1000" step="any" required></label>
 <label>Start of working space — chainage (m)<input name="worksStart" type="number" min="-10000000" max="10000000" step="any" value="0" required></label>
 </div>
 <label class="generator-check"><input name="hasHardShoulder" type="checkbox"> Hard shoulder present (nearside closures involving it need a separate design)</label>
 <label class="generator-check"><input name="congestion" type="checkbox"> Congestion likely — extend the dual-carriageway advance signing</label>
 <label class="generator-check"><input name="scopeConfirmed" type="checkbox" required> I confirm this is a simple straight-road case without affected junctions, level crossings, guide islands, contraflow, multiple closed lanes or mobile working. A competent designer must check visibility, access, swept paths, queues, pedestrian provision and authority requirements.</label>
 <p>Intermediate portable-signal warning signs are marked provisional for site siting. Temporary speed-limit signing, extra shoulder/access/pedestrian runs, lamps and spare cones are not included in the core quantities. Two-way WAIT HERE separation must not exceed 300 m. Standard lane-closure profiles require 3.6–4 m lanes.</p>
 <button type="submit">Calculate and draw editable draft</button><p data-generator-status role="status">Or use the manual tools below to start from scratch.</p>
 </form>
 <p data-cone-count role="status">Cone symbols in current sketch: 0.</p>
 <details class="calculation-details" data-calculation-details hidden><summary>Calculated distances, sign schedule and cone quantities</summary><pre data-calculation-report></pre><button type="button" data-report disabled>Save calculation report</button></details>

 <div class="toolbar"><label>Tool<select data-tool><option value="select">Select / move</option><option value="road">Road</option><option value="cone">Cone</option><option value="barrier">Barrier</option><option value="sign">Sign</option><option value="lights">Traffic lights</option><option value="works">Works area</option><option value="label">Label</option></select></label><label>Label / sign text<input data-label maxlength="120" value="Works access"></label><button type="button" data-undo>Undo</button><button type="button" data-delete>Delete selected</button><button type="button" data-clear>New drawing</button></div>
 <p class="help">Drag to draw a road, barrier or works area. Click to place other items. Choose Select / move, then drag an item to reposition it. Select an item to edit its text. The grid is a sketch guide, not a distance scale.</p>
 <svg data-canvas viewBox="0 0 1000 650" role="img" aria-label="Traffic-management draft drawing canvas" tabindex="0"><defs><pattern id="tm-grid" width="25" height="25" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M 25 0 L 0 0 0 25" fill="none" stroke="#e0e7e5" stroke-width="1"/></pattern></defs><rect width="1000" height="650" fill="url(#tm-grid)"/><g data-entities></g></svg>
 <details><summary>Place items using coordinates (keyboard alternative)</summary><div class="coordinates"><label>X<input data-x type="number" min="30" max="950" value="100"></label><label>Y<input data-y type="number" min="30" max="570" value="100"></label><label>End X<input data-x2 type="number" min="30" max="950" value="400"></label><label>End Y<input data-y2 type="number" min="30" max="570" value="200"></label><button type="button" data-add>Add item using selected tool</button><label>Select item<select data-selection><option value="-1">None</option></select></label></div></details>
 <div class="actions"><button type="button" data-dxf>Export DXF</button><button type="button" data-pdf>Export PDF</button><button type="button" data-project>Save editable project</button><label class="file-label">Open project<input data-open-project type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label></div>
 <p data-save-status role="status"></p><p data-drawing-status role="status"></p></section>
 <section id="tm-upload" aria-labelledby="upload-heading"><h3 id="upload-heading">Upload an existing drawing</h3><label>Choose a drawing (maximum 20 MB)<input data-upload type="file" accept=".dxf,.dwg,.pdf,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.webp,.gif,.bmp"></label>
 <p>Files stay in this tab’s memory and are <strong>not uploaded to a server or saved to your account</strong>. Reloading or closing the tab removes them. Keep your own original. Uploading does not attach a drawing to checkout.</p>
 <p>DXF: basic ASCII LINE, CIRCLE, TEXT and straight LWPOLYLINE previews only; other entities, blocks, dimensions, styling and external references may be missing. PDF viewing depends on your browser. PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF and BMP images can be previewed. <strong>DWG cannot be viewed or edited here</strong>: download the original and use a compatible CAD viewer, or export DXF, PDF or an image from your CAD application for preview.</p>
 <p data-upload-status role="status"></p><a data-original hidden>Download original</a><div data-preview class="preview"></div></section>
 <p class="work-pack-link">Need the accompanying work pack? <a href="#tm-form">Continue to the existing work-pack form ↓</a></p>
</section>
<script>import { bindTrafficDrawing } from '../lib/traffic-management/client';bindTrafficDrawing();</script>
